# Deploy Workflow

The user never builds locally. Do NOT run local build commands.

- ❌ Do not run `npm run build`, `npm --prefix client run build`, `tsc -b`, `vite build`, or any local build/preview step to "verify" changes.
- ✅ After making code changes, just `git add`, `git commit`, and `git push origin main`. Heroku auto-deploys from `main`.
- Verification happens on the live site (auto-deploy), not locally.

To catch errors without a full build, use lightweight, non-build checks instead:

- Use the `ReadLints` tool on changed files.
- Use type/lint checks only if they don't trigger a bundle build.

If a build is ever truly required, ask the user first.
